# AAText preferences - OPTIONAL.
#
# Without this file AAText works out of the box: every TrueType font
# installed on the system (fonts with a .otag file in FONTS:) is drawn
# antialiased, in every size, with the code page from its .otag file.
# Bitmap fonts (topaz, XEN, ...) are left alone.
#
# To change anything, copy this file to ENVARC:AAText.prefs (and
# ENV:AAText.prefs) and edit it.

# Automatic TrueType detection via .otag files (default on).
#auto off

# Real metrics for detected fonts (default off): use the TrueType
# font's own character widths instead of squeezing letters into the
# bitmap font's cells. Text looks more natural, but window layouts
# change: start AAText before other programs (WBStartup); windows that
# were already open keep their old layout until reopened.
# Fixed-width fonts (Shell, editors) always keep their cells.
#real on

# Gamma for the antialiasing edge (0.5 - 4.0, default 0.8).
# Lower values make text thinner and crisper, higher values bolder.
#gamma 0.8

# Glyph cache size in KB (32 - 16384, default 256). Least recently used
# glyphs are dropped when it is full.
#cache 256

# Programs AAText must not touch (Workbench program name or Shell command
# name, case does not matter). Several lines are allowed.
#blacklist FinalWriter TypeSmith

# Some programs draw text into hidden bitmaps first (e.g. docks, gauges).
# "on" draws those with the Workbench screen colours; colours may be wrong
# if the program is not on the Workbench screen. Default off.
#offscreen on

# Explicit mappings (rarely needed): draw a font with a TrueType file,
# e.g. a bitmap font, or a font whose .otag is not found.
#
#   bitmapfont  size  ->  ttf file  [pixelsize] [real]
#
# - "bitmapfont" is the font name without .font; use double quotes if it
#   contains spaces. "size" must match exactly.
# - pixelsize is optional; without it AAText picks the size whose
#   character widths best match the bitmap font.
# - "real" uses the TrueType widths for this font only.
#
#topaz  8  ->  FONTS:_ttf/DejaVuSansMono.ttf

# Character set for explicit mappings: latin1 (default) or latin5
# (Turkish). Detected fonts use the code page of their .otag instead.
#charset latin5
